{
  "//": [
    "Editor-only config — this project has no TypeScript and no build step.",
    "It exists so VS Code resolves the `@/` (browser) and `#` (Node) aliases.",
    "",
    "At runtime those aliases are resolved by:",
    "  @/  -> the <script type='importmap'> in each public/*.html  -> /js/",
    "  #   -> the `imports` field in package.json                  -> ./src/",
    "Keep all three in sync when adding a mapping."
  ],
  "compilerOptions": {
    "checkJs": false,
    "module": "esnext",
    "target": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "baseUrl": ".",
    "paths": {
      "@/*": ["public/js/*"],
      "#features/*": ["src/features/*"],
      "#lib/*": ["src/lib/*"]
    }
  },
  "include": ["public/js/**/*.js", "src/**/*.js"],
  "exclude": ["node_modules"]
}
